  "mathematical_claims": [
    "For every finite additive-gap set A, |X_A(T)| <= 2*|A|*pickupDiagonal(T) <= 4*|A|*T^2.",
    "The gap bound depends on cardinality, not gap magnitude.",
    "The cutoff floor(exp(epsilon*T/2)) is all-positive-rate.",
    "After excluding selected gaps, every pair touching the final M births costs at most 16*M^3/floor(exp T)^2 when 2*M<=floor(exp T).",
    "At M=floor(exp(2T/3)) the terminal-birth sector is eventually at most 64.",
    "The remaining signed core has gap greater than exp(epsilon*T/2)+O(1) and maximum index at most floor(exp T)-exp(2T/3)+O(1).",
    "A dense constant positive Gram saturates the degree-times-energy factor; this is a method obstruction, not a Möbius counterexample."
  ],
